# One host, one scheme. Google crawled www and http copies of every page and
# filed them as "alternative page with proper canonical tag" - harmless, but a
# 301 is what it wants. Rules with a full URL match on host and scheme.
https://www.hourstally.com/* https://hourstally.com/:splat 301
http://www.hourstally.com/* https://hourstally.com/:splat 301
http://hourstally.com/* https://hourstally.com/:splat 301

/index.html / 301
/time-to-decimal.html /time-to-decimal 301
/privacy.html /privacy 301
/about.html /about 301
/how-it-counts.html /how-it-counts 301
